course: dictionary
lesson: 14327
title: Observed: watched and noticed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Observed is the past form of observe. To observe something means to watch it carefully, often so you can learn from it. «The scientist observed the plant every day for a month.» She watched closely, day after day, so observed means watched carefully.
explain: Observed can also mean noticed or saw something. «Mia observed a fox creeping across the garden.» Mia saw the fox, and she probably noticed how quietly it moved. In science, observed results are the things you watched happen in an experiment, and you write them down.
explain: Observed can be formal too. It can mean said or remarked, or it can mean kept a rule or custom. «Everyone observed a minute's silence.» That means they kept the custom of being quiet together. Ask yourself: is the word about watching, noticing, or keeping a rule?
fact: Observe is the verb, and observed is its past form, so it describes something that happened before.
fact: «Observed» means watched or looked at carefully, often to learn something.
fact: «Observed» can also mean noticed or saw something, as in «observed that the door was open».
fact: In formal speech, «observed» can mean kept a rule or custom, as in «observed the speed limit».
fact: Useful phrases: «observed that», «was observed», and «observed results» in science.
exercise: «The scientist observed the plant every day for a month.» What does observed mean here? | *Watched carefully | Painted | Shouted at | Forgot about
exercise: «Mia observed a fox creeping across the garden.» What does observed mean here? | Chased | Drew a map of | Ate | *Noticed or saw
exercise: Priya says observed always means spying on someone. What is the best answer? | No, it means very tired | *No, it can mean watched carefully, noticed, or kept a rule | Yes, but only in science | Yes, it always means spying
test: «Everyone observed a minute's silence for the lost sailors.» What does observed mean here? | *Kept a custom | Lost | Shouted | Ran away
test: «The police officer observed that the shop door was open.» What does observed mean here? | Hid | Sang | *Noticed | Painted
exam: Which sentence uses observed to mean watched carefully in a science test? | She went home early and forgot the test | *She observed the results and wrote them down in her notebook | She sang a song to the plants | She ate her lunch while the test was running
